subthemes.text:
[17] The Appellants argue that:
* The RPD erred by failing to conduct a subjective fear and credibility analysis prior to assessing IFA;
* The RPD erred in concluding that the agents of persecution do not have the reach and power to harm the Appellants in Port Harcourt;
* The RPD erred by failing to consider the challenges of Appellants as a single parent family, and the circumstances of the PA when considering her employability, and ability to settle with minor children in Port Harcourt is undermined by lack of indigene.

